{{WikiProject advice|wikiproject=WikiProject AI Cleanup|WP:AITALKSIGNS|WP:LLMTALKSIGNS}}
This is a list of writing and formatting conventions typically found in comments written by Wikipedia users who are (or have been) suspected of using [[large language model]]s or similar technology to write content, with real examples taken from talk pages and other discussion pages. Comments suspected of having been pasted from an LLM may be collapsed via {{tl|collapse AI}} per [[WP:AITALK]]. Using AI to write comments is considered [[WP:LLMDISRUPT|disruptive]], and editors who do so may be blocked if they persist after being warned.

Although several of the tells mentioned at [[Wikipedia:Signs of AI writing]] (including [[WP:AIBOLD|boldface]], [[WP:AIDASH|em dashes]], [[WP:AICURLY|curly apostrophes and quotation marks]], [[WP:AIPARALLEL|negative parallelisms]], [[WP:AILIST|vertical lists]], [[WP:MARKDOWN|Markdown]], and the [[WP:RO3|rule of three]]) often appear in such comments, this project page only includes tells that typically do not appear in content added to articles or drafts.

Moreover, this list is ''descriptive'', not ''prescriptive''; it consists of observations, not rules. Advice about formatting or conduct can be found in the [[WP:Talk page guidelines|talk page guidelines]], but does not belong on this page.

== Content ==

===<span class="anchor" id="Emphasis on quality"></span><span class="anchor" id="Emphasis on good faith"></span><span class="anchor" id="Emphasis on adherence"></span><span class="anchor" id="Assurances"></span> Canned assurance of quality, good faith, and adherence to policies and guidelines===
{{shortcuts|WP:AIASSURANCE|WP:AIASSURE|WP:AIADHERENCE|WP:AIADHERE}}
{{tmbox|image=none|text=Words to watch: {{strong|''align(s) with Wikipedia's aim/goal(s)'', ''adhere(s) to Wikipedia's policies/guidelines/standards'', ''I am/remain committed to ...'', ''I assure you that ...'', ''my intention/goal is to ...'', ''I understand ...'', ''Moving forward, I will ...''}} }}

Most people on Wikipedia want others to believe that they're here for the right reasons and are willing to follow the rules, and may insist that they make their contributions with such rules in mind. AI chatbots, however, have a strong tendency to communicate this in a specific way: invoking policies, guidelines, and standards as a broad, formal, and abstract whole, as in [[legalese]], and often using "[[WP:AIVOCAB|AI vocabulary]]" to do so. 

'''Examples'''
{{blockquote|{{fmbox|image=none|text=
I have a genuine interest in contributing to the knowledge and accuracy of information available on Wikipedia, particularly in the area of dogs. I have conducted extensive research and have insights that I believe could enhance the quality and comprehensiveness of the existing content on the "Dog" article.

{{highlight|I understand}} the importance of {{highlight|adhering to Wikipedia's guidelines and policies}}, and {{highlight|I am committed to}} contributing in a responsible and constructive manner. {{highlight|My intention is to}} provide well-referenced and reliable information that {{highlight|aligns with Wikipedia's standards.}}

If granted permission, I would approach the editing process {{highlight|with the utmost care and respect for Wikipedia's community guidelines.}}
}}|From [[Talk:Dog/Archive 8#Semi-protected edit request on 26 February 2024|this February 2024 edit request]] at [[Talk:Dog]]}}

{{blockquote|{{fmbox|image=none|text=
{{highlight|I assure you that}} my intentions are {{highlight|aligned with Wikipedia's principles}} of neutrality, verifiability, and reliability. I strive to {{highlight|adhere to all content and editing guidelines}}, ensuring the information provided is accurate, well-sourced, and encyclopedic.
}}|From [[Wikipedia:Identifying LLM unblock requests#company page deleted from wiki i did nothing wrong write a unblock request so i can edit company page again|this demonstrative example]] at [[Wikipedia:Identifying LLM unblock requests]]}}

{{blockquote|{{fmbox|image=none|text=
{{highlight|I can assure you that}} the article and our comments are the result of human effort and collaboration. {{highlight|Anon and I are committed to}} creating informative and balanced content that {{highlight|adheres to Wikipedia's guidelines}}. [...] Let's work together to ensure that our article contributes meaningfully to the climate change discourse.
----
Chloe and I are ready to provide any additional clarification or context that might be needed. The article is now more focused on the economic impacts and includes a range of viewpoints on technology and policy, with a clear human-centered narrative. We've also ensured that all sources are credible and properly cited. [...] {{highlight|Our ultimate goal is to}} create a valuable resource that {{highlight|aligns with Wikipedia's high standards}} and sparks important conversations about our planet's future.
}}|From [[Wikipedia:WikiProject Articles for creation/Help desk/Archives/2024 December 8#c-162.156.70.174-20241208202000-Qcne-20241208195600|these December 2024 AfC help desk comments]]}}

{{blockquote|{{fmbox|image=none|text=
Thank you for reaching out and highlighting the conflict of interest (COI) guidelines. I appreciate Wikipedia’s commitment to maintaining neutrality, verifiability, and reliability in all articles.

{{highlight|I acknowledge the importance of}} avoiding undue influence when contributing to topics directly related to an individual or organization. {{highlight|My intent is to}} ensure that information [...] remains accurate, neutral, and supported by credible sources. {{highlight|I am committed to adhering to Wikipedia’s COI policies}} and, {{highlight|moving forward, I will}}:

- Refrain from directly editing the article and instead suggest edits on the talk page using reliable third-party sources.

- Ensure full disclosure of my affiliation when discussing potential edits, {{highlight|in compliance with Wikipedia’s transparency guidelines}}.

- Avoid promotional content or external link spamming, ensuring that all suggested content {{highlight|aligns with Wikipedia’s standards of neutrality and verifiability}}.
