== Language and grammar ==

=== <span class="anchor" id="Itemization"></span> Itemization of content policies ===
{{shortcut|WP:ITEMIZE}}
Whenever LLM users bring up a few of Wikipedia's policies and guidelines, they tend to mention each one by name. In some cases, each policy's title is written in [[WP:AITITLECASE|title case]] and its corresponding shortcut is mentioned in parentheses. This has sometimes been the case when the user attempts to either [[WP:AIADHERE|assure others that their content is compliant]] or [[WP:ORCC|request input]] to help them ensure such compliance. Editors might name-drop policies and guidelines in this fashion to exaggerate their comprehension of the rules and make a point that their reasoning is based on them, even though AI chatbots [[WP:AIFICTPOLICY|sometimes get them wrong]].

'''Examples'''
